<title>SPAIN: TABLE - Spain CPI consensus sees 0.18 pct July rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Spain CPI consensus sees 0.18 pct July rise.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a simple average of CPI forecasts contributed by private economists:</p>
<p>	   Mth  Change   Range     Pvs  Yr-yr  Range   97/96 Ave</p>
<p>CPI  (%) Jul  +0.18% (0.06/0.3)  0.0  1.61 (1.48/1.8) 1.87 1.90</p>
<p>Core (%) Jul  +0.10% (0.0/0.15)  0.2  1.84 (1.7/1.92) 1.89 2.01</p>
<p>Sources: Intermoney, AFI, Argentaria, Santander Inv, ICAE, Merrill Lynch, Beta Capital, C. Madrid, Benito y Monjardin, BBV.</p>
<p>NOTE - The National Statistics Institute will publish the official figure on August 13. Core inflation excludes energy and unprocessed food.</p>
</text>
